{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe handler prices CloudWatch token counts with a Cost-Explorer-derived rate table\nmatched to models by substring and suffix heuristics. That layer produced four\ndefects in the twelve days after deployment (2026-09-12): a direction-suffix\ncollision in `_rate_for`/`_match`, a `_normalise` label/id mismatch, the\n`BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES` allowlist omitting five live services, and\n`MARKETPLACE_TOKEN_SUFFIXES` handling only CamelCase. Two reached production\nunalarmed, one for seven days. They are one class — matching model identifiers\nagainst billing labels — so this story deletes the class, not the instances.\n\n## Approach\n\nPrice every token at a ceiling rate for its direction, above the highest rate\nobserved on this account, so the estimate is an upper bound and the cap cannot fire\nlate. Per UTC day:\n\n    spend = max( sum over regions and the four token metrics of\n                   undimensioned CloudWatch Sum * CEILING[metric],\n                 ce_spend )\n\nCost Explorer stays in enforcement: it is the only signal covering Bedrock spend\nthat publishes no token metric, and it is orthogonal to all four defects.\n\nThe undimensioned series is requested with `Dimensions: []` (omitting the key is\nnot equivalent). It matched the per-ModelId sum exactly over 2026-09-14 to 09-24,\n930,831,660 tokens both ways — an external-system assumption AC 1 re-verifies.\n\nAn all-empty read is ambiguous: both a metrics gap and the idle/new-day state\nrelease depends on. CE cannot disambiguate it, lagging 8-24h. The handler persists\nthe day's high-water token total keyed by UTC date; the criteria give the four\ndispositions. It governs release only, so a gap cannot manufacture a trip.\n\nCeiling pricing over-estimates cheap models — the cheapest here by two orders of\nmagnitude, and two bill nothing for cache-write — so an embedding job can trip the\ncap at a fraction of intended spend. Accepted; the remedy is an exact-match\n`{ModelId: rate}` override, equality only. Fixtures, the drift guard, the README\nand the `ListMetrics` re-grant are the dependent story be3d-712b-c1ac-442b.\n\n## Figures\n\nBill figures are barred from the tracker; the tickets branch is public. Inputs:\n\n- intended daily cap: `var.bedrock_daily_cap_usd`, unchanged here.\n- `CEILING[d]`: 1.25x the highest per-token rate for direction `d` across all\n  Bedrock services in the trailing 60 days of CE.\n- threshold: the intended daily cap scaled by the median of\n  (undimensioned tokens x CEILING) / (CE Bedrock total), over UTC days in that\n  window whose CE total exceeds one twentieth of the cap.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The undimensioned-versus-per-ModelId equivalence is re-run over a fresh\n  ten-day window and is exactly equal per region and metric; on divergence the work\n  halts and escalates. Checked: output recorded as a comment here.\n- [ ] `_refresh_rates`, `_rate_for`, `_seed_for`, `_normalise`,\n  `_strip_billing_region`, `_marketplace_rate_key`, `_rate_key_for_ce_group`,\n  `SEED_RATES`, `RATE_OVERRIDES`, `BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES`,\n  `MARKETPLACE_TOKEN_SUFFIXES`, `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`,\n  `MARKETPLACE_TOKENS_PER_RATE_UNIT` and the `TOKEN_METRICS` multipliers are absent.\n- [ ] The now-unreferenced `re` and `typing.Literal` imports are removed.\n- [ ] The module docstring no longer describes a derived rate table, seed rates,\n  `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K` or a daily refresh.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` is rewritten: the harness\n  stops setting `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`, stubbing `_refresh_rates` and constructing\n  `metered_estimated`, and no test references a removed symbol.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend` issues exactly four undimensioned `GetMetricData` queries per\n  region, each sending `Dimensions: []`, and calls no `list_metrics`.\n- [ ] `cloudwatch:ListMetrics` is removed from the role's `ReadSpendSignals`\n  statement, leaving `ce:GetCostAndUsage` and `cloudwatch:GetMetricData`.\n- [ ] `CEILING` gives one rate per token metric, each at least the highest for that\n  direction over the trailing 60 days of CE, with the derivation commented beside it.\n- [ ] Enforcement compares `max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend)`.\n- [ ] `_ce_spend_today` classifies by predicate — service equals `Amazon Bedrock`\n  or ends with the Bedrock Edition suffix — and matches all ten live services.\n- [ ] The day's high-water token total is persisted keyed by UTC date.\n- [ ] An empty read with today's key present and zero-valued may release.\n- [ ] An empty read after a nonzero reading that day holds the deny.\n- [ ] An empty read with today's key absent and a deny attached holds the deny.\n- [ ] A partial-region failure holds the deny.\n- [ ] Any exception from a metered or CE read fails closed.\n- [ ] `bedrock_spend_cap.tf` carries the threshold and warning values derived above.\n- [ ] The `SEED_RATES`, `RATE_OVERRIDES`, `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K` and\n  `RATE_WINDOW_DAYS` env entries are deleted with whichever `variable` or `locals`\n  blocks are left unreferenced; `terraform plan` shows exactly those deletions, the\n  IAM removal, and the threshold and warning changes, and `terraform validate` passes.\n- [ ] `state[\"rates\"]`, `state[\"rates_day\"]`, `metered_estimated`, `MeteredRate`\n  and its `RateSource` alias, and the `\" (estimated)\"` rendering are removed.\n\n## Testing\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -q`\nproves every criterion except the Terraform ones, proved via\n`python3 scripts/terraform_prod.py plan --out <scratch>/plan.tfplan` and\n`terraform validate`, and the unused imports, proved by `make lint`.\n`make lint`/`make typecheck` gate commits; `make verify` runs before push.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`DRY_RUN=true` halts attach and detach while keeping the function observable. Full\nback-out: revert the change and re-run the mediated plan and apply, restoring prior\ncode, env and IAM exactly."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1790303461686932124,"uuid":"2164c18a-cf47-4403-9319-1f1e1ac12928"}